 \begin{solutionbox} \begin{enumerate}[label=\protect\circled{\color{white}\arabic*}]
\item  \faCodeFork\ \begin{bf}Nonelectrolyte:\end{bf}  When the aqueous solution of that substance does not conduct electricity. In general terms, these electrolytes present low conductivities, lower than 10$\mu$S$\cdot $cm$^{-1}$.
\item \faCodeFork\ \begin{bf}Weak electrolyte:\end{bf}When the aqueous solution of that substance conducts electricity poorly. In general terms, these electrolytes present medium conductivities, between 10-1000$\mu$S$\cdot $cm$^{-1}$.
\item \faCodeFork\ \begin{bf}Strong electrolyte:\end{bf} When the conductivity of the aqueous solution of that substance is high. In general terms, these electrolytes present large conductivities, larger than 1000$\mu$S$\cdot $cm$^{-1}$.
\end{enumerate}
\end{solutionbox} 
 


 